1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,158
In two minutes, Dr. Vale will demonstrate

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:04,680
an ancient torture machine on live television.

3
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:06,640
He has rehearsed the screaming.

4
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:08,580
He has not read the instructions.

5
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,460
Mina has read them.

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:11,760
That's why she's running.

7
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:16,300
Two hours earlier, this was still supposed to be the greatest discovery of his career.

8
00:00:17,430 --> 00:00:20,268
The year is three thousand twenty six.

9
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:24,210
Under an old shopping center, Vale and Mina find a room full of heavy objects.

10
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:30,170
There are handles to pull, platforms to push, and benches beneath enormous bars.

11
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:31,370
A torture chamber.

12
00:00:31,730 --> 00:00:32,570
Or a training room.

13
00:00:32,980 --> 00:00:34,180
Training to do what?

14
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,200
They lift the object, then put it exactly where it was.

15
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:39,520
He peers into a smaller room at the back.

16
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:40,180
A desk.

17
00:00:40,440 --> 00:00:41,460
Two plastic chairs.

18
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,460
A locked drawer.

19
00:00:42,840 --> 00:00:43,860
We'll examine that later.

20
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,180
He calls the museum.

21
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,640
A banner goes up before the dust has settled.

22
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:49,380
ANCIENT CRUELTY.

23
00:00:49,860 --> 00:00:51,320
LIVE DEMONSTRATION TODAY.

24
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:52,600
We haven't finished looking.

25
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:53,550
Then look quickly.

26
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:56,440
Mina restores a security recording.

27
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,120
A man lies beneath a bar.

28
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,440
His face tightens.

29
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,960
Another man stands over him.

30
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:01,720
One more.

31
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:02,400
There.

32
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:03,200
A confession.

33
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:04,180
That's encouragement.

34
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:06,100
The bar returns to its supports.

35
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:08,080
The two men laugh and shake hands.

36
00:01:08,460 --> 00:01:09,540
Complicated society.

37
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:11,780
Mina advances the recording.

38
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,620
People enter through the front door.

39
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,580
They leave through the same door.

40
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,680
One comes back carrying special shoes.

41
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:18,720
They can leave.

42
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:19,960
They bring equipment.

43
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,700
They appear to want to be here.

44
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,680
Play the part with the screaming again.

45
00:01:24,810 --> 00:01:28,210
Inside a locker, Mina finds a membership card and a receipt.

46
00:01:28,630 --> 00:01:29,810
Vale stops talking.

47
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:31,070
He reads the payment.

48
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:32,130
Then the renewal.

49
00:01:32,490 --> 00:01:33,490
Then the payment again.

50
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:34,270
They paid?

51
00:01:35,070 --> 00:01:35,550
Every month.

52
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:37,050
For the suffering?

53
00:01:37,410 --> 00:01:38,630
For something.

54
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:40,110
Let's find out what.

55
00:01:40,570 --> 00:01:41,768
She turns the card over.

56
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:43,850
There is a paragraph of tiny writing.

57
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:47,290
Vale takes a photograph of the price and hurries away.

58
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:50,250
At the museum, his new headline is even larger.

59
00:01:50,690 --> 00:01:52,330
HUMANS PAID TO BE TORTURED.

60
00:01:52,710 --> 00:01:55,610
You found one new fact and made the conclusion worse.

61
00:01:56,740 --> 00:02:00,300
Mina follows the same member through recordings made weeks apart.

62
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:03,420
On the first day, his coach removes weight from the bar.

63
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,580
On a later day, the man completes that exercise more easily.

64
00:02:06,880 --> 00:02:07,380
Watch him.

65
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:08,600
Not the metal.

66
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,260
Vale watches.

67
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:12,060
The bar is still a bar.

68
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:14,160
The person handling it has improved.

69
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,160
They were training.

70
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:17,560
Resistance makes muscles work against a load.

71
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:20,360
Repeated training, with recovery, can make them stronger.

72
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:24,780
As capacity improves, a suitable challenge can increase gradually.

73
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,480
Progress takes time.

74
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,620
It isn't one terrible afternoon.

75
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,440
Then why is there a heavier weight?

76
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:33,260
A challenge that was hard can become easier.

77
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:36,340
That doesn't mean everyone starts with the same one.

78
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,478
A different clip shows the coach stopping

79
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:40,840
a painful movement and changing the exercise.

80
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,300
And pain isn't the goal.

81
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:46,250
Vale retreats to his strongest evidence.

82
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:47,490
A treadmill.

83
00:02:48,230 --> 00:02:50,690
He points at the recording of a woman walking on it.

84
00:02:51,070 --> 00:02:52,910
Explain why they trapped her on a road.

85
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:54,830
She controls the speed.

86
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:56,190
She's exercising.

87
00:02:56,610 --> 00:03:00,530
Brisk walking makes the heart beat faster and breathing work harder.

88
00:03:01,350 --> 00:03:04,250
Regular aerobic activity can improve fitness over time.

89
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:08,030
Moving across a room isn't required for the body to be doing work.

90
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:10,210
They invented vehicles to avoid walking.

91
00:03:10,710 --> 00:03:11,570
Then purchased walking?

92
00:03:12,030 --> 00:03:13,870
You're beginning to understand the species.

93
00:03:14,230 --> 00:03:18,808
A museum assistant wheels the restored treadmill toward the demonstration stage.

94
00:03:18,810 --> 00:03:21,070
Vale follows it.

95
00:03:21,250 --> 00:03:23,290
Mina stays behind to finish reading the card.

96
00:03:24,320 --> 00:03:25,460
Now the cameras are ready.

97
00:03:25,740 --> 00:03:26,618
The banner is enormous.

98
00:03:26,620 --> 00:03:29,360
Vale steps onto the stationary belt.

99
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,840
He raises a solemn hand.

100
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:33,580
Today, I will experience what these people endured.

101
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,200
Mina runs onto the stage.

102
00:03:35,480 --> 00:03:35,820
Wait.

103
00:03:35,880 --> 00:03:37,660
You haven't attached the safety clip.

104
00:03:38,110 --> 00:03:40,228
She shows him the stop control, attaches the

105
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:42,848
clip, and starts the belt at a slow walking pace.

106
00:03:42,850 --> 00:03:45,970
Vale grips the rails, expecting catastrophe.

107
00:03:46,790 --> 00:03:47,630
He takes a step.

108
00:03:47,730 --> 00:03:48,370
Then another.

109
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:49,950
When does the torture begin?

110
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:51,720
It doesn't have to.

111
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:54,340
He lowers his prepared expression of agony.

112
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:57,340
Behind him, his own headline fills the screen.

113
00:03:58,470 --> 00:04:00,570
Then why not send a machine to lift the weights?

114
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:02,708
Mina picks up a small demonstration weight.

115
00:04:02,710 --> 00:04:06,510
A museum robot takes it, lifts it, and returns it to the stand.

116
00:04:06,810 --> 00:04:07,930
Did that train your muscles?

117
00:04:08,290 --> 00:04:10,090
Vale looks at his arm.

118
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:11,070
Then at the robot.

119
00:04:11,450 --> 00:04:13,370
A machine can move a load for you.

120
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:15,670
That doesn't give your muscles the training stimulus.

121
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:20,430
Exercise asks your body to do the work so it can adapt over time.

122
00:04:20,810 --> 00:04:22,890
They weren't paying because the metal needed moving.

123
00:04:23,350 --> 00:04:25,470
She puts the member's recordings on the screen.

124
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:28,950
This time, she includes what happened outside the gym.

125
00:04:30,080 --> 00:04:32,300
The man carries groceries up steps.

126
00:04:32,780 --> 00:04:35,138
The woman from the treadmill takes a walk with a friend.

127
00:04:35,140 --> 00:04:39,240
The coach holds the door while someone leaves, tired but laughing.

128
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:42,620
Exercise can support everyday physical function.

129
00:04:43,260 --> 00:04:46,440
What people need, what they can do, and how they improve varies.

130
00:04:47,140 --> 00:04:48,260
A gym is one option.

131
00:04:48,760 --> 00:04:51,280
Home exercises and outdoor activity can count too.

132
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:54,620
So they came here to make things outside this room easier.

133
00:04:55,080 --> 00:04:55,640
Some did.

134
00:04:55,960 --> 00:04:57,980
And some probably just liked coming.

135
00:04:58,340 --> 00:05:00,598
Vale looks from the ordinary lives on the screen

136
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,720
to the sensational headline above him.

137
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:04,498
The broadcast is still live.

138
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:07,480
Vale reaches toward the broadcast control.

139
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,020
He could stop the feed.

140
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,360
Instead, he moves his hand to the treadmill's stop button.

141
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:13,920
We need to change the sign.

142
00:05:15,050 --> 00:05:17,128
Later, the new exhibit is almost ready.

143
00:05:17,130 --> 00:05:20,790
Vale has crossed out TORTURE CHAMBER and written GYM.

144
00:05:21,590 --> 00:05:23,390
Mina puts the membership card beside it.

145
00:05:23,770 --> 00:05:25,510
Then what was in the little office?

146
00:05:25,970 --> 00:05:27,390
Remember the tiny writing?

147
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:29,430
She restores one final recording.

148
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:32,010
The member walks up to the office desk.

149
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:33,130
I'd like to cancel.

150
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:33,910
Of course.

151
00:05:34,090 --> 00:05:34,930
Did you bring the form?

152
00:05:35,390 --> 00:05:36,350
The one on the website?

153
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:37,990
The one you request by mail.

154
00:05:38,450 --> 00:05:39,490
Can I request it here?

155
00:05:39,950 --> 00:05:40,270
Online.

156
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:43,890
Vale slowly picks up his discarded sign.

157
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:47,978
On opening day, visitors pass the weights, the treadmill,

158
00:05:47,980 --> 00:05:50,440
and the recordings explaining how people trained.

159
00:05:50,860 --> 00:05:52,720
At the back is a reconstructed office.

160
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:53,700
A desk.

161
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:55,200
Two plastic chairs.

162
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,360
A locked drawer.

163
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:59,280
Above its door, Vale has hung his original sign.

164
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,300
You finally found somewhere for it.

165
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:04,820
In the end, Dr. Vale did discover a torture chamber.

166
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:06,980
He'd just been pointing at the wrong room.
